{"id":"2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all","date":"2026-11-25","topic":"ai","region":"americas","headline":"Human Brains Process All Languages in Similar Ways","source":{"name":"MIT News","url":"https://news.mit.edu/2026/many-languages-one-common-neural-code-1123"},"accent":"uk","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"People around the world speak many different languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t1-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":3.64,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.64,0.9,1.2,1.7,2.16,2.68]},{"text":"Scientists at MIT studied how humans hear stories.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t1-1.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","M","S","V","O"],"dur":4.26,"times":[0.0,0.42,0.84,1.24,2.12,2.54,3.0,3.36]},{"text":"A new computer program helped with this work.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t1-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","M","M","M"],"dur":2.6,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.26,0.68,1.18,1.56,1.88,2.04]},{"text":"The computer showed how human minds understand words.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t1-3.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","M","S","S","V","O"],"dur":3.65,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.34,0.78,1.1,1.42,1.88,2.62]},{"text":"Every person uses the same system for meaning.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t1-4.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":3.47,"times":[0.0,0.24,0.68,1.12,1.4,1.66,2.1,2.52]}],"bands":{"core1000":97,"core1800":3,"ngsl":0,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":0},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"speak","title":"Simple Present Tense","note":"We use the simple present tense to state general facts or truths. Here, it describes a universal fact about people around the world."},{"i":1,"focus":"how humans hear stories","title":"Indirect Question as Object","note":"A question word like 'how' can introduce a noun clause that acts as the object of a main verb. In this sentence, the clause acts as the object of 'studied'."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"People across the world speak thousands of very different languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t2-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":4.77,"times":[0.0,0.34,0.68,1.0,1.32,1.82,2.34,2.96,3.28,3.8]},{"text":"Researchers at MIT studied brain activity from 21 different languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t2-1.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":5.57,"times":[0.0,0.34,0.7,1.08,1.96,2.32,2.84,3.34,3.84,4.66]},{"text":"Andrea Gregor de Varda and Evelina Fedorenko used new computer models.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t2-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":5.86,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.98,1.16,1.66,2.26,2.8,3.54,4.08,4.5,4.98]},{"text":"Volunteers listened to stories so the models predicted their brain activity.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t2-3.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":4.69,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.84,1.24,1.72,2.32,2.46,2.7,3.22,3.72,3.96]},{"text":"This work will help doctors discover brain problems in many people.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t2-4.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","V","O","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":4.48,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.4,0.7,0.94,1.38,1.88,2.3,2.72,3.2,3.44]}],"bands":{"core1000":81,"core1800":11,"ngsl":2,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":6},"grammar":[{"i":3,"focus":"so","title":"Conjunction Showing Result","note":"The conjunction 'so' introduces a clause expressing a result or purpose. Here, it connects the action of listening to stories with the outcome of predicting brain activity."},{"i":4,"focus":"will help","title":"Future Tense with Will","note":"The modal verb 'will' forms the simple future tense to express expected future outcomes. In this sentence, it refers to the beneficial goal of the ongoing research."}]},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"Human languages have developed thousands of unique patterns and grammatical rules over time.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":5.96,"times":[0.0,0.32,0.76,1.2,1.54,2.2,2.64,2.96,3.46,3.9,4.46,4.86,5.42]},{"text":"Scientists at MIT have now discovered that human brains process all these languages similarly.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-1.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","M","V","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","M"],"dur":6.72,"times":[0.0,0.38,0.82,1.26,2.02,2.22,2.64,2.98,3.32,3.88,4.62,5.06,5.3,5.9]},{"text":"Lead researcher Andrea Gregor de Varda used multilingual AI models that analyze many languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","S","V","O","O"],"dur":6.62,"times":[0.0,0.18,0.54,1.26,1.82,1.94,2.42,2.94,3.72,4.18,4.66,5.02,5.34,5.84]},{"text":"Participants speaking 21 different languages listened to stories while scientists recorded their brain responses.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-3.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":6.92,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.84,1.44,2.04,2.6,3.16,3.56,4.06,4.56,5.04,5.52,5.96,6.39]},{"text":"The team built encoding models, which are software tools that estimate human brain activity.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-4.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","O","O","S","V","C","C","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":5.44,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.32,0.64,0.9,2.12,2.26,2.42,2.7,3.2,3.5,3.82,4.32,4.72]},{"text":"A model trained on French even predicted brain responses in Vietnamese listeners accurately.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-5.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","M","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":5.42,"times":[0.0,0.0,0.24,0.58,0.82,1.18,1.82,2.22,2.58,3.2,3.54,3.84,4.78]},{"text":"Senior author Evelina Fedorenko believes this shared system helps us understand core word meanings.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t3-6.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","S","S","S","V","O","C","C","C","C"],"dur":6.88,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.66,1.28,1.94,2.52,2.86,3.18,3.68,4.06,4.26,4.88,5.28,5.76]}],"bands":{"core1000":75,"core1800":16,"ngsl":3,"tsl":1,"nawl":2,"beyond":3},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"have developed","title":"Present Perfect Tense","note":"The present perfect tense (have + past participle) connects a past action to the present. It shows that languages began developing in the past and continue to possess these patterns."},{"i":4,"focus":"which are software tools","title":"Non-defining Relative Clause","note":"A non-defining relative clause starts with 'which' after a comma to give non-essential extra information. It describes 'encoding models' without limiting their definition."}]},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"Although human languages vary dramatically in structure, human brains process meaning through a shared system.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-0.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","V","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":7.57,"times":[0.0,0.38,0.82,1.55,1.92,2.66,3.0,3.98,4.36,4.84,5.46,5.9,6.32,6.44,6.72]},{"text":"In a study published in Nature Neuroscience, MIT researchers examined native speakers of 21 diverse languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-1.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":8.08,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.12,0.36,0.76,1.08,1.46,2.86,3.16,3.92,4.52,4.98,5.5,5.88,6.36,6.94]},{"text":"Postdoctoral researcher Andrea Gregor de Varda combined brain scan data with outputs from multilingual artificial intelligence models.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":8.6,"times":[0.0,0.4,1.04,1.8,2.36,2.48,2.9,3.44,4.0,4.34,4.74,5.1,5.54,5.88,6.58,7.04,7.56]},{"text":"These computational tools created encoding models, which are specialized computer programs that predict human brain activity.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-3.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","S","V","C","C","C","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":7.36,"times":[0.0,0.16,0.52,1.38,1.72,2.08,3.28,3.42,3.6,3.94,4.52,5.06,5.48,5.8,6.24,6.64]},{"text":"Study participants listened to recorded audio passages from \"Alice in Wonderland\" while their neural signals were recorded.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-4.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","S","V","V"],"dur":6.66,"times":[0.0,0.24,0.72,1.12,1.48,1.76,2.24,2.7,3.18,3.46,3.74,3.94,4.82,4.98,5.22,5.72,6.08]},{"text":"Surprisingly, an encoding model trained only on French successfully predicted brain responses in Vietnamese listeners.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-5.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","M","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":7.36,"times":[0.0,1.0,1.12,1.3,1.76,2.16,2.56,2.82,3.18,3.88,4.64,5.02,5.54,5.92,6.24]},{"text":"Senior author Evelina Fedorenko stated that this unexpected alignment reveals a shared neural code for understanding.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-6.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":7.24,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.64,1.28,1.92,2.48,2.8,3.0,3.4,4.1,4.68,5.02,5.38,5.72,6.2,6.5]},{"text":"Researchers hope these insights will help clinicians diagnose brain disorders across global patient populations.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t4-7.m4a","roles":["S","V","S","S","V","V","O","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":6.45,"times":[0.0,0.28,0.64,0.88,1.32,1.62,1.82,2.14,2.68,3.24,3.74,4.22,4.6,5.04]}],"bands":{"core1000":57,"core1800":20,"ngsl":9,"tsl":3,"nawl":6,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"Although","title":"Subordinating Conjunction of Concession","note":"'Although' introduces a subordinate clause expressing contrast. It sets up a surprising contrast between structural differences in languages and universal brain processing."},{"i":4,"focus":"were recorded","title":"Passive Voice","note":"The passive structure (were + past participle) shifts focus onto the action's recipient ('neural signals') rather than the person performing the action. This is common in formal scientific descriptions."}]},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"Despite the vast structural diversity across human speech, the brain appears to rely on a universal code to process meaning.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-0.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":8.5,"times":[0.0,0.38,0.78,1.16,1.86,2.38,3.06,3.42,4.28,4.6,4.82,5.14,5.4,5.56,5.96,6.04,6.46,7.1,7.56,7.88]},{"text":"A groundbreaking study from MIT demonstrates that remarkably diverse languages activate our neural language networks in nearly identical ways.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-1.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":9.77,"times":[0.0,0.04,0.34,1.1,1.38,1.8,2.86,3.3,3.8,4.48,5.22,5.88,6.32,6.58,7.12,7.52,8.02,8.28,8.82]},{"text":"Lead author Andrea Gregor de Varda and senior author Evelina Fedorenko evaluated brain activity across native speakers of 21 distinct languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":10.05,"times":[0.0,0.2,0.44,1.06,1.52,1.66,2.08,2.5,2.78,3.24,3.82,4.52,5.24,5.86,6.3,6.9,7.22,7.76,8.04,8.52,9.18]},{"text":"The research team utilized multilingual large language models, extracting numerical patterns to compare against human functional brain imaging data.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-3.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":8.9,"times":[0.0,0.04,0.18,0.66,1.1,2.06,2.5,3.06,3.86,4.3,4.72,5.4,5.9,6.16,6.58,7.06,7.58,7.94,8.32]},{"text":"Volunteers listened to translated passages from \"Alice in Wonderland\" while scientists carefully recorded neural activity within the left hemisphere.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-4.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","M","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":8.49,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.72,1.04,1.6,1.96,2.52,2.82,3.1,3.32,4.24,4.68,5.2,5.78,6.16,6.8,7.34,7.56,7.74]},{"text":"Using these measurements, the team created encoding models capable of forecasting complex brain responses to previously unheard linguistic inputs.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-5.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":8.95,"times":[0.0,0.2,0.38,1.26,1.32,1.5,2.0,2.22,2.98,3.54,3.86,4.4,4.92,5.42,6.02,6.36,6.82,7.5,7.96]},{"text":"Remarkably, an encoding model trained exclusively on French data predicted brain activity patterns in individuals listening to Vietnamese.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-6.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":8.23,"times":[0.0,0.76,0.96,1.06,1.62,2.02,2.64,3.1,3.4,3.78,4.38,4.8,5.24,5.62,5.96,6.44,6.98,7.28]},{"text":"This cross-linguistic alignment indicates that human communication relies on a shared underlying representation of semantic meaning across all cultures.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-7.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","M","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":9.32,"times":[0.0,0.22,0.98,1.36,2.2,2.52,2.84,3.44,4.04,4.44,4.52,4.86,5.4,6.3,6.86,7.12,7.7,8.16,8.56]},{"text":"Beyond advancing basic neuroscience, these findings could help refine diagnostic tools for neurological disorders and protect endangered languages.","voice":"voice/2026-11-25-ai-human-brains-process-all/t5-8.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","S","S","V","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":8.9,"times":[0.0,0.18,0.66,1.06,2.28,2.36,2.7,3.02,3.2,3.68,4.18,4.74,5.06,5.28,6.2,6.72,7.1,7.52]}],"bands":{"core1000":62,"core1800":11,"ngsl":11,"tsl":2,"nawl":7,"beyond":7},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"Despite","title":"Preposition of Concession","note":"'Despite' is a preposition used to express contrast. Unlike 'although', which introduces a full subject-verb clause, 'despite' must be followed by a noun phrase."},{"i":3,"focus":"extracting numerical patterns to compare against human functional brain imaging data","title":"Participle Phrase as Adverbial Modifier","note":"A present participle phrase (-ing phrase) can modify the main clause to show a simultaneous action or method. Here, it explains how the research team utilized the AI models."}]}},"glossary":[{"word":"multilingual","lemma":"multilingual","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌmʌltiˈlɪŋɡwəl/","definition":"using or involving several different languages","tiers":["t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"predicted","lemma":"predict","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prɪˈdɪktɪd/","definition":"stated that something would happen in the future","tiers":["t2","t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"encoding models","lemma":"encoding model","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɛnˈkoʊdɪŋ ˈmɑdəlz/","definition":"computer programs that estimate brain responses to language","tiers":["t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"alignment","lemma":"alignment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈlaɪnmənt/","definition":"a matching position or relationship between things","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"hemisphere","lemma":"hemisphere","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɛmɪˌsfɪr/","definition":"one half of the brain","tiers":["t5"]},{"word":"semantic","lemma":"semantic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/sɪˈmæntɪk/","definition":"relating to meaning in language","tiers":["t5"]},{"word":"diagnostic","lemma":"diagnostic","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌdaɪəɡˈnɑstɪk/","definition":"used for identifying an illness or medical condition","tiers":["t5"]}],"words":{"people":{"l":"person","p":"noun","i":"/ˈpipəl/","d":"human be